01:14:07.140 --> 01:14:13.830
Balazs Nemethi: And parallel to this, I discovered that ICANN offers a process called a cognitive priority process.

532
01:14:14.420 --> 01:14:20.660
Balazs Nemethi: Which… Prioritizes a community application over any other type of applications.

533
01:14:21.170 --> 01:14:28.930
Balazs Nemethi: So, as long as a community is able to meet the requirements set forth by ICANN of what a community is in a pointing system.

534
01:14:30.030 --> 01:14:41.219
Balazs Nemethi: If it's accepted, then there is no bidding process, so regardless of any other economic actors who would want to, kind of, like, win the domain through a bidding.

535
01:14:41.680 --> 01:14:46.410
Balazs Nemethi: The domain just gets assigned to the community application, and…

536
01:14:47.030 --> 01:15:03.330
Balazs Nemethi: effectively, that's the end. They become the registry. So, kind of, like, learning about this and having some degree of background in identity, I was like, this is awesome, we have to do this. So I started Agent Community with a very initial, strong focus on

537
01:15:03.580 --> 01:15:15.449
